L0005: Raw identifier syntax is unavailable

Rust raw identifiers such as r#match are not part of Locus. The lexer rejects the raw prefix instead of silently treating a keyword as a name. Choose an ordinary, non-reserved identifier.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/raw_identifier.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```rust
// A raw identifier.
fn first(r#match: u8) -> u8 { 1 }
```

Language, as built: [1.0:2](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.0:2).
